    "summary": "Reproduced the input/readback discrepancy in a fresh editor map. For Colored Wall, the hex field visibly accepted `ff0300`; after OK, placing the wall, picking that placed wall, and reopening its picker, the field showed `ff0200ff` (RGB `ff0200` with opaque alpha). Repeating the enter/OK/reopen path for Colored Floor also changed `ff0300` to `ff0200ff`. Earlier UI checks also matched the selective pattern: Floor `ff0400` read back as `ff0300ff`, while control `ff0500` remained `ff0500ff`.",
    "oracle": {
      "kind": "sequence",
      "description": "The reporter states that, after entering listed color strings and placing tiles adjacent to one another, some inputs were reported as being accepted by the editor as a different value. Reported nonmatching input -> accepted mappings are: ff0300 -> ff0200; ff0400 -> ff0300; ff0800 -> ff0700; ff0900 -> ff0800; ff0c00 -> ff0b00; ff0d00 -> ff0c00; ff1100 -> ff1000; ff1200 -> ff1100; ff1500 -> ff1400; ff1600 -> ff1500; ff1700 -> ff1600; ff1a00 -> ff1900; ff1b00 -> ff1a00; ff1f00 -> ff1e00; ff2000 -> ff1f00. The other entries in the supplied ff0000, ff0100, \u2026, ff2000 table were reported as unchanged. The report references a screenshot and a save archive, but their contents are not included in the supplied payload for independent verification.",
